{"title":"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d74121afb82b85afd4a4902e208519cc17aa83f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{3}=6(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"19\" />. Prove that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a692cc9be7a64044ca8771effcbd14fe0199e102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+ax+a^{2}-6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> has no real solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant\" title=\"Discriminant\">discriminant</a> of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a692cc9be7a64044ca8771effcbd14fe0199e102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+ax+a^{2}-6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0a530a99cdcfad7e355a5d7e051953d4dc38b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - 4(a^2 - 6) = -3a^2 + 24.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"19\" />  In order for the quadratic equation to have no real solution, the discriminant must be less than zero, so we need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0abaff3ebf930531554fbf7aac2b8e78f7454a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3a^2 + 24 &lt; 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />  That means we need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b545a4678a9dd3f85b8764cfcf496f717f0d4fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 2\\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nAssume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c88fa0ad5176bb6193c14c9b6f3f200d03374642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le 2\\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" />  Rearranging the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d74121afb82b85afd4a4902e208519cc17aa83f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{3}=6(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"19\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/82943924ed3950d03353e6858783646633347405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(a^2 - 6) = 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54f7beac9077dd3b40f434ddc844a2a63a75c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a &lt; \\sqrt{6},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179efe0de0cf0056d791910b28f5fa019cc9555f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(a^2 - 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" /> would be negative, making the equality fail.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574826a30c973d8901dfbb41b66e53688f8df7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{6} \\le a \\le 2\\sqrt{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/1819a8d986d1d7449aea7795e3c1a9785c3ba7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a^2 - 6 \\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/48983b4aaf9e25758b2c07731c651c1311444ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le a(a^2 - 6) \\le 4\\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />  However, that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/1873bf27522cdb8d96f9e3b434c37fbdaec1a200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(a^2 - 6) \\le 4\\sqrt{2} &lt; 6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"21\" /> so the equality also fails.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proof_by_contradiction\" title=\"Proof by contradiction\">proof by contradiction</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71df1b44d6caa4b0f798d48ff8ee72da386e4cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so the discriminant of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a692cc9be7a64044ca8771effcbd14fe0199e102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+ax+a^{2}-6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> is negative.  That means the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a692cc9be7a64044ca8771effcbd14fe0199e102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+ax+a^{2}-6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> has no real solution.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively it is possible to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52d6e197d04166486d27a808d36cc87dfa90953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a^2 &gt; 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16b2d9c22f84ad75bec4c165ce30c358596fc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. However, the original expression also rearranges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/3289f34adc8863d059f53a395612fcc702e00caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 = \\frac{6(a+1)}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"40\" />. Therefore it is enough to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a219e484ab106363ce380a4e9f3801b51f40e59d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(a+1)&gt;8a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b689abbbf1e231f489d17f9fd1ec5a19e9fe61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. Evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/3/7230920a133b86893c8f65665e5e7beb0797b70c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965d03ac07aa731815fd43e68385996fb8129d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> shows the intersection point is between these values, and there are clearly no more because the cube is convex on positive numbers. That means the quadratic in the question has no real solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO\" title=\"2007 JBMO\">2007 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017133153\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 184/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 839/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 43/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5344/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.549      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    8.549      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16664:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017133153 and revision id 217671. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}